# Kimpor Kang — Construction Portfolio Website

## 1. Project Purpose

Personal single-page portfolio for **Kimpor Kang**, a junior Civil Engineering
student at Paragon International University (Phnom Penh) who works as Project
Coordinator at **Singbuild Construction Co., Ltd.** (design & build contractor,
est. 2015). The site presents real construction / interior fit-out project
experience, skills, side projects, and contact info. Target audience: employers,
clients, and engineering contacts in Phnom Penh and beyond.

## 2. Tech Stack & Constraints

- **Plain HTML5 + CSS3 + vanilla JavaScript** — no frameworks, no bundlers,
  no npm dependencies, no build step.
- Fonts loaded from Google Fonts CDN: `Archivo` (headings), `Inter` (body),
  `IBM Plex Mono` (labels/mono). Site degrades gracefully to system fonts
  offline.
- Deployable as-is on any static host. On Vercel it needs **zero config**
  (no framework, output = repo root, `index.html` entry).
- Do NOT introduce a framework, package.json, or build pipeline unless the
  user explicitly asks — the deliberate simplicity is a design decision.

## 3. File Structure

```
Kimpor-Portfolio-Website/
├── index.html              # The ENTIRE site (single page, ~420 lines)
├── css/
│   └── style.css           # All styling: tokens, layout, responsive (~20 KB)
├── js/
│   └── script.js           # All interactivity (IIFE, strict mode, ES5-safe)
├── images/
│   ├── projects/           # 15 project JPGs referenced by project cards
│   ├── portrait.jpg        # Owner's headshot (white studio background)
│   ├── portrait-cutout.png # Generated: transparent-background portrait
│   └── _PUT-PHOTOS-HERE.txt# Internal note about photo placement
├── tools/
│   └── cutout.py           # Removes the white background from portrait.jpg
├── README.md               # Human docs: run, photo map, edit guides
└── kimpor-portfolio.skill  # This file
```

## 4. Design System (css/style.css `:root`)

| Token | Value | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `--navy` | `#0d2841` | logo block, burger, hero strip, footer, badges, rules |
| `--navy-2` | `#14395c` | hovers on navy, text links |
| `--navy-deep` | `#08192a` | headings, hero veil, hero fallback background |
| `--paper` | `#ffffff` | page background |
| `--soft` | `#f4f6f8` | alt sections + portrait frame background |
| `--line` | `#e4e8ec` | hairline borders and dividers |
| `--text` / `--dim` | `#22303c` / `#6c7a88` | body / secondary text |
| `--menu` | `#95a1ad` | inactive nav menu cells |
| `--ok` / `--live` | `#2f855a` / `#c07a17` | status colours (dots render `#5fd39a` done, `#f0b34e` ongoing, `#7dc4ff` ahead) |
| `--bar` | `72px` | top-bar height (60px under 640px) |
| `--w` | `min(1200px, 92%)` | content width |

- Headings, menu, labels: **Jost** (300–600). Body copy: **Inter**. Both from
  Google Fonts with system fallbacks.
- Hero tagline **"Drawn to Build"** is rendered twice: a huge stroke-only
  "ghost" (`-webkit-text-stroke: 1px rgba(255,255,255,.3)`, uppercase) layered
  behind the solid white title.
- Typography system: uppercase micro-labels with 0.16–0.32em letter-spacing,
  hairline rules instead of cards-with-shadows where possible, square corners
  (no border radius anywhere).
- Re-theming: colours live only in `:root`; README documents the palette.

## 5. Page Sections (index.html, in order)

1. **Top bar** — navy logo block (SVG twin-chevron mark, "KIMPOR KANG",
   "Civil Engineering · Phnom Penh"), equal-width white menu cells divided by
   hairlines (`.menu-item[data-nav]`), and a navy hamburger block
   (`#navToggle`) at the far right. Menu cells hide below 980px.
2. **Slide-down panel** (`#navPanel`) — the hamburger toggles a full-width
   panel with numbered section links (`.panel-link`) plus contact meta.
3. **Hero** — full-bleed `images/projects/fengfu-office.jpg` under a navy veil;
   eyebrow "Kimpor Kang · Phnom Penh, Cambodia"; the double-rendered
   **"Drawn to Build"** title (ghost stroke text behind solid white); sub-line;
   two buttons (`.btn-solid`, `.btn-line`); navy bottom strip with the domain.
4. **Stats band** — four hairline-divided cells: 15 projects / 11 completed &
   handed over / 4 ongoing / 5 sectors.
5. **About** (`#about`, label `01`) — portrait frame (`#portraitImg` on a
   blueprint-grid background with a navy name plate) beside the bio and a
   hairline `.facts-list` (degree, experience, focus, languages, location).
6. **Projects** (`#projects`, label `02`, soft-grey) — filter buttons
   (All 15 / Completed-Handover 11 / Ongoing 4) + 15 `.card` tiles carrying
   `data-status`; each card has a 16:10 photo, `.badge` with `.dot`, title,
   type line and description. Missing photos fall back to the
   `.media-placeholder` initials tile.
7. **Skills** (`#skills`, label `03`) — groups A/B (`.skill-group`) with
   `.chip-list` hairline rows.
8. **Side Projects** (`#side-projects`, label `04`, navy section) — two
   translucent `.side-card`s: SB Grab Code Tracker, Manpower Reporting
   Automation.
9. **Contact** (`#contact`, label `05`) — navy-topped `.contact-card` with
   label/value rows. **Contains placeholders**: `[Add your email]`,
   `[Add your phone]`, `[Add your LinkedIn URL]` — update both the visible
   text and the `mailto:` / `tel:` / href attributes.
10. **Footer** — navy bar with JS-injected year and back-to-top link.

Scroll-reveal: elements carry `.reveal`; JS adds `.is-visible` via
IntersectionObserver. Sections use `scroll-margin-top` to clear the sticky bar.

## 6. JavaScript Behavior (js/script.js)

Single IIFE, `'use strict'`, ES5-compatible (var, function expressions) with
modern APIs guarded:
1. Menu panel (`#navToggle` / `#navPanel`): toggles `.is-open`, keeps
   aria-expanded/aria-label in sync, closes on link click and on Escape.
2. Scroll reveal via IntersectionObserver; fallback shows everything.
3. Active nav highlighting: second IntersectionObserver over `section[id]`
   toggles `.is-active` on every `[data-nav]` link with a matching hash
   (covers both menu cells and panel links).
4. Project status filter: `.filter-btn[data-filter]` toggles `.is-hidden` on
   `#projectsGrid .card` by matching `data-status`; re-adds `.is-visible` so
   filtered cards don't re-animate.
5. Footer year via `new Date().getFullYear()`.

Keep new JS in the same IIFE style; no external libraries.
